353</fpage><lpage>374</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003808-Cartmill1"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cartmill</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Lemelin</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Schmitt</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Support polygons and symmetrical gaits in mammals.</article-title><source>Zoological Journal of the Linnean Society</source><volume>136</volume><fpage>401</fpage><lpage>420</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003808-Hedrick1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hedrick</surname><given-names>TL</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>&#x0201c;DLT Data Viewer 2&#x0201d;, Digitizing and DLT in MATLAB.</article-title></citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn fn-type="conflict"><p><bold>Competing Interests: </bold>The authors have declared that no competing interests exist.</p></fn><fn fn-type="financial-disclosure"><p><bold>Funding: </bold>This work was supported by NSF awards DBI-0630670 to KLB and BCS-0452217 to DS.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>